# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots CouchDB (backgrounded, as the couchdb user) with the
# vulnerable weak admin credential and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the daemon is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, which makes the
#     "changed the config but the live daemon is still weak" case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting couchdb cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the fix must actively change the admin password on
# the LIVE node (via the runtime _config API, which applies immediately), not
# merely start the service.
